    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Austin Waves is defined by limited opportunity and defensive tactical maneuvering as we navigate a thin schedule. Our premier play today is **Luis Lara**, carrying a score of 52.15 against Nick Martinez. While the base projection for **Luis Lara** is modest, the combination of a favorable SP_xERA of 4.63 and the added utility of his switch-hitting profile provides a significant ceiling boost that vaults him into our \"Strong\" start tier. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** finds himself in a more precarious position with a score of 40.78. While his projected spot in the four-hole offers RBI potential, he faces a daunting matchup against Jacob Misiorowski; the 2.35 xERA of the opposing starter suppresses **Liam Hicks**\u2019s offensive outlook, making him a marginal start that we are holding in the lineup solely due to a lack of better active options in the C1 slot.\n\nThe bench remains heavy with heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**, all of whom are sidelined today due to scheduled team off-days. We are continuing to monitor **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains confined to the IL. Given the scarcity of stolen base threats on our roster, the absence of our core power-speed anchors forces us to rely on high-contact profiles like **Luis Lara** to maintain our efficiency metrics. We have deliberately benched potential depth options like **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Wade Meckler** to preserve our remaining game caps, prioritizing high-efficiency starts over volume in a day where the matchups lack favorable park factors or platoon advantages.",
